## Z — EXAM PATTERN: group by key, sum values, find max per group

split on : to get user and "process^cpu"
use SUBSEP to create a 2D array key (user + process)
sum CPU per user+process pair
in END, scan all keys to find top process per user

| Construct | Meaning |
|-----------|----------|
| `index(str, char)` | position of char in str (1-based, 0 if not found) |
| `substr(str, start, len)` | extract substring (start is 1-based) |
| `key = a SUBSEP b` | SUBSEP = special separator for 2D array keys |
| `split(key, arr, SUBSEP)` | splits SUBSEP key back into arr[1], arr[2] |
| `!(user in seen)` | "in" tests if key exists in array |

