      if (i > maxcol) maxcol = i
      if (minrow == 0 || NR < minrow) minrow = NR
      if (NR > maxrow) maxrow = NR
    }
  }
}
END {
  for (r=1; r<=NR; r++) {
    out = ""
    n = split(lines[r], chars, "")
    for (i=1; i<=n; i++) {
      if (r >= minrow && r <= maxrow && i >= mincol && i <= maxcol) {
        out = out "0"     # inside inner bbox: zero it out
      } else if (chars[i] == "*") {
        out = out "x"     # outer border: * becomes x
      } else {
        out = out chars[i]  # spaces and anything else: unchanged
      }
    }
    print out
  }
}
'
```

- First pass accumulates all lines and finds the bounding box of `x` characters
- Second pass (END) replays each line with character-level substitutions
- The bounding box check `r>=minrow && r<=maxrow && i>=mincol && i<=maxcol` correctly fills the ENTIRE inner rectangle region with zeros, not just its border
- `mincol == 0` guard handles the case where no `x` is found (won't happen in valid inputs)

